Z||000000||bHooper||03-09-2000||08:19 PM||||i hate to bother you guys for your opinions  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> , but i am at a decision making point on my car, and would like some advice.  i have spent the past week debating between buying a  formula, or repairing my car... here is the take on that.<P>my 86.5 GT has been sitting since 8/96 without a tranny (5 speed).  a local shop took it apart after the destruction, and it was never reasembled (couldnt find the right tranny at the time).  i just got through putting a a socket on the crank at it turns several "ratch's" b4 compresion builds up (either way)... so it appears that the engine is fine.<P>as for the tranny, i have 2 options: 1) a getrag replacement (Yes I have found one  in decent shape at a reasonable price) and 2) a local yard has a '86 4 cyl 5 speed that has never been touched.  not one thing is missing from the car!!<P>either option will cost me about $400.  with option 2, i get new carpet, and parts to sell to you guys (please dont be selfish with your replies  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">, plus i get to "learn" how to reasemble the tranny by takeing it apart,  and with option 1, i get the proper tranny solution to my car.  of course, this doesnt count the cost of the clutch and pp, $130-250, depending on my choices there.  or anything else i may run across.<P>so, after typeing a book full... what do you guys think i should honestly do?<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||03-09-2000||08:50 PM||||Do you know that the 4cly 5 sp is not the same tranny as the V6 5sp?||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||03-09-2000||08:57 PM||||the 4 cyl cars used the isuzu 5 speed.  wheras the 6 cyl cars used the getrag munice 5 speed.  theory has it that the isuzu cant handle the torque of the 6 cyl.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||03-10-2000||01:06 AM||||That's what GM said.  the had warranty claims to consider, tho.  it wouldn't look good for them if a bunch of tranny's broke.  So long as you don't power shift it too often it should hold up fine.  I've read of people using it behind a V8 and it held up.<P>Are the gear ratio's different?  If it were me I'd get the getrag, especially since 86.5's 5 speeds are rare.  and fun, too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Uaana||03-10-2000||02:29 AM||||Now you guys tell me the five speeds are rare<BR>I went and dumped off my 85 SE with a 5sp<BR>for free just to get it out of the lot before<BR>mgt threw a fit..||||reg||8
Z||000005||bHooper||03-10-2000||06:50 AM||||standard, thats what im thining.  i like to "work" a tranny when i go play in the mountains.  there is no doubt the getrag is preferable, but with the 4 cyl car, i could offset som of my cost!||||reg||1
Z||000006||ChadMan||03-10-2000||09:29 AM||||Hmm...GM says the Isuzu won't handle the torque of the V6.  Meanwhile, V8 Archie claims it can handle up to 300 hp with no problems (I haven't seen him publish a torque rating).<P>I personally have never known anyone who has had an Isuzu 5-sp fail.  But I have seen two V8 Fieros with 5-sp Isuzus and talked to both owners, and both said they have yet to experience any problem.  And SCCA FIERO is running a V6/Isuzu combo without problems (and he's into autocrossing too).<P>So I'm guessing you're probably OK with the Isuzu if weekly drag racing isn't your bag.||||reg||1
Z||000007||batboy||03-10-2000||11:02 AM||||Uaana, the "rare" Getrag 5 speed was not used in the 85 models. Your tranny was probably the Isuzu 5 speed and I bet it was matched with a four cylinder, because the V6 Fieros in 85 had the 4 speed Muncies.||||reg||1
Z||000008||bHooper||03-10-2000||05:59 PM||||well, i went to make a offer on the parts car today.  he came off of his price $50... so i could get the car for $350.  but i am still concerned, who knows if the tranny is any good?!  it could be notch, have a bad synchro, ect.  i think i'm going to buy the getrag and rebuild my car the right way!  even if it takes me a little longer, and cost a little more!<P>thats what i should do!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
